---
title: Apply Answers
id: interrupts-apply-answers
order: 6
description: "Read a generic interrupt answer on the continuation run and apply it to the next model turn."
keywords:
  - tanstack ai
  - onInterruptResolution
  - toolResume
  - generic interrupt
  - parentRunId
  - createCapability
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The user approved a plan or typed a note. You need that value on the server\nbefore the next model call. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onInterruptResolution"},{"type":"text","value":" is where you read it. It\ndoes not change config. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" is where you apply it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By the end of this page you know when the resolution hook runs, what it can\nreturn, and how to turn the answer into a prompt, a tool list, or a stop."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Define and emit the interrupt first. See "},{"type":"link","href":"./generic","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generic Interrupts"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"two-chat-calls","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Two "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" calls"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The pause spans two runs. One user-visible turn. Two "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" calls."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call 1 (pause)."}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onInterruptBoundary"},{"type":"text","value":" returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ interrupts }"},{"type":"text","value":". The run\nends with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_FINISHED"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outcome: interrupt"},{"type":"text","value":". The resolution hook does\nnot run."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call 2 (resume)."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The client starts a new request after\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resolveInterrupt()"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cancel()"},{"type":"text","value":". The body includes:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a new "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runId"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parentRunId"},{"type":"text","value":" set to the paused run"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resume"},{"type":"text","value":" with the answers. Each generic item also has "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata"},{"type":"text","value":" with the\noriginal request ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack:interruptContinuation"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":" sends those fields for you. If you POST by hand, include all three.\nIf "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resume"},{"type":"text","value":" is present and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parentRunId"},{"type":"text","value":" is missing, the server throws."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A hand-built generic resume item looks like this:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { wrapGenericInterruptContinuation } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nconst resumeItem = {\n  interruptId: 'generic-1',\n  status: 'resolved' as const,\n  payload: { approved: true },\n  metadata: wrapGenericInterruptContinuation({\n    v: 1,\n    definitionId: 'review-plan',\n    key: 'turn-1',\n    batchIndex: 0,\n    reason: 'review',\n    message: 'Review the plan',\n  }),\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"sequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant Client\n    participant Server\n\n    Client->>Server: first chat() request\n    Server-->>Client: RUN_FINISHED outcome interrupt\n    Client->>User: interrupts array\n    User->>Client: resolveInterrupt or cancel\n    Client->>Server: second chat() with parentRunId and resume\n    Note over Server: onInterruptResolution runs here\n    Server-->>Client: continue, cancel tools, or stop","lang":"mermaid"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"exact-place-in-the-second-call","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exact place in the second call"}]},{"type":"code","value":"setup\nonConfig                 (phase is init)\nonInterruptResolution    (phase is still init)\nonStart\nthen stop, or continue the agent loop"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The hook runs "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"once"}]},{"type":"text","value":", at the start of the continuation. It does not run at\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeModel"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"afterModel"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeTools"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"afterTools"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.phase"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'init'"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.iteration"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":". No model call has started."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The hook runs once per batch. Two cards in one pause still produce one hook\ncall with both answers."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The hook does not run on the first user message. It does not run for a\ntool-approval or client-tool batch that has no generic interrupt."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If that continuation pauses again, that is a third "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call. The hook\nruns again at the start of that third call."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"read-the-typed-answers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read the typed answers"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type { ChatMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { reviewPlan } from './interrupts'\n\nexport const applyReview: ChatMiddleware<unknown, typeof reviewPlan> = {\n  name: 'apply-review',\n  onInterruptResolution(_ctx, resumedInterrupts) {\n    for (const result of resumedInterrupts.for(reviewPlan)) {\n      if (result.status === 'resolved' && !result.response.approved) {\n        return { toolResume: 'stop' }\n      }\n    }\n  },\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resumedInterrupts.for(reviewPlan)"},{"type":"text","value":" keeps the response type for that\ndefinition"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resumedInterrupts.all()"},{"type":"text","value":" returns every registered answer"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resumedInterrupts.all(reviewPlan, otherDefinition)"},{"type":"text","value":" narrows to those\ndefinitions"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each item is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resolved"},{"type":"text","value":" (with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"response"},{"type":"text","value":") or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cancelled"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-the-hook-can-return","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What the hook can return"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolResume"},{"type":"text","value":" to decide what happens to "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"pending tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" from the\npaused turn:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Value"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Effect"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"continue"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run the pending tools"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cancel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mark the pending tools as cancelled. Do not run them"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"End the run after "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onStart"},{"type":"text","value":". No tools. No model call"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When more than one middleware returns a value, the engine keeps the stricter\none. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop"},{"type":"text","value":" wins over "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cancel"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cancel"},{"type":"text","value":" wins over "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"continue"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If a generic interrupt shares a batch with client tools, the client does not\nrun those client tools until "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolResume"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"continue"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cancel"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop"},{"type":"text","value":"\nskip them. After "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"continue"},{"type":"text","value":", the engine emits the client-tool wait again."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"continue"},{"type":"text","value":", the engine picks up from the phase that paused:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"First run paused at"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next step"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeModel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The model call"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"afterModel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools, if the model asked for them"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeTools"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool execution"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"afterTools"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The next model turn (the tools already ran)"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-the-hook-cannot-change","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What the hook cannot change"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onInterruptResolution"},{"type":"text","value":" cannot change config. It cannot change the model or\nthe adapter."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These fields change only from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" (or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onStructuredOutputConfig"},{"type":"text","value":"):"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"systemPrompts"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The user answer is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"not"}]},{"type":"text","value":" added to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":" by itself. If the model must\nsee the note, you add it."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"apply-the-answer-in-onconfig","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Apply the answer in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Order on the continuation:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"phase: 'init'"},{"type":"text","value":". The answers are not applied yet."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onInterruptResolution"},{"type":"text","value":". Read the answers and store them on the run."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"phase: 'beforeModel'"},{"type":"text","value":". Return the new prompts, tools, or\nmessages."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Store the answer in a "},{"type":"link","href":"../advanced/middleware#capabilities","children":[{"type":"text","value":"middleware capability"}]},{"type":"text","value":".\nThe value lives on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx"},{"type":"text","value":" for this "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call. Another middleware can\ndeclare "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requires"},{"type":"text","value":" and read the same note. Two overlapping "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" calls do\nnot share the value."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you list the capability in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"provides"},{"type":"text","value":", you must provide it in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setup"},{"type":"text","value":".\nYou do not have the user answer yet. Provide an empty box first. Write the\nanswer in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onInterruptResolution"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createCapability, type ChatMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { reviewPlan } from './interrupts'\n\nexport const reviewNote = createCapability<{ note?: string }>()('review-note')\nexport const [getReviewNote, provideReviewNote] = reviewNote\n\nexport const reviewMiddleware: ChatMiddleware<unknown, typeof reviewPlan> = {\n  name: 'review-plan',\n  provides: [reviewNote],\n  setup(ctx) {\n    provideReviewNote(ctx, {})\n  },\n  onInterruptBoundary(ctx) {\n    if (ctx.phase !== 'beforeModel') return\n    if (ctx.parentRunId) return\n    return {\n      interrupts: [\n        reviewPlan.interrupt({\n          key: 'initial-plan',\n          reason: 'review-required',\n          message: 'Review the proposed plan.',\n          payload: {\n            title: 'Release plan',\n            changes: ['Add search'],\n          },\n        }),\n      ],\n    }\n  },\n  onInterruptResolution(ctx, resumed) {\n    const [result] = resumed.for(reviewPlan)\n    if (result?.status !== 'resolved') return\n    provideReviewNote(ctx, { note: result.response.note })\n    if (!result.response.approved) {\n      return { toolResume: 'stop' }\n    }\n  },\n  onConfig(ctx, config) {\n    if (ctx.phase !== 'beforeModel') return\n    const note = getReviewNote(ctx).note\n    if (!note) return\n    return {\n      systemPrompts: [\n        ...config.systemPrompts,\n        `User review note: ${note}`,\n      ],\n    }\n  },\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Register the object on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat({ middleware: [reviewMiddleware] })"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A later middleware can read the same note:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { type ChatMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { getReviewNote, reviewNote } from './review-plan'\n\nexport const applyVoice: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: 'apply-voice',\n  requires: [reviewNote],\n  onConfig(ctx, config) {\n    const note = getReviewNote(ctx).note\n    if (!note) return\n    return {\n      systemPrompts: [...config.systemPrompts, `Voice note: ${note}`],\n    }\n  },\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Other hooks that can change behavior, but not this resume payload:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onBeforeToolCall"},{"type":"text","value":" can rewrite args, skip a tool, or abort"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChunk"},{"type":"text","value":" can rewrite or drop stream events"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onShouldContinue"},{"type":"text","value":" can return "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" to stop the loop with a normal finish"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"../advanced/middleware","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Middleware"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for those hooks."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"persistence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Persistence"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With "},{"type":"link","href":"../persistence/chat-persistence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"chat persistence"}]},{"type":"text","value":", the hook still runs\nat the same moment: after init "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"},{"type":"text","value":", before "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onStart"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Persistence rebuilds the pending requests from the store and clears\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"config.resume"},{"type":"text","value":" so the engine does not rebuild them from client history. You\nstill read answers from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resumedInterrupts.for(definition)"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"register-both-sides","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Register both sides"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The continuation needs the same definitions and the same middleware as the\npaused run. Forward "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parentRunId"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resume"},{"type":"text","value":" from the request."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// app/api/chat/route.ts\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { reviewMiddleware } from '../../chat-middleware'\nimport { reviewPlan } from '../../interrupts'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request)\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    threadId: params.threadId,\n    runId: params.runId,\n    ...(params.parentRunId ? { parentRunId: params.parentRunId } : {}),\n    ...(params.resume ? { resume: params.resume } : {}),\n    interrupts: [reviewPlan],\n    middleware: [reviewMiddleware],\n  })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"two-chat-calls","text":"Two chat() calls","level":2},{"id":"exact-place-in-the-second-call","text":"Exact place in the second call","level":2},{"id":"read-the-typed-answers","text":"Read the typed answers","level":2},{"id":"what-the-hook-can-return","text":"What the hook can return","level":2},{"id":"what-the-hook-cannot-change","text":"What the hook cannot change","level":2},{"id":"apply-the-answer-in-onconfig","text":"Apply the answer in onConfig","level":2},{"id":"persistence","text":"Persistence","level":2},{"id":"register-both-sides","text":"Register both sides","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe user approved a plan or typed a note. You need that value on the server\nbefore the next model call. `onInterruptResolution` is where you read it. It\ndoes not change config. `onConfig` is where you apply it.\n\nBy the end of this page you know when the resolution hook runs, what it can\nreturn, and how to turn the answer into a prompt, a tool list, or a stop.\n\nDefine and emit the interrupt first. See [Generic Interrupts](./generic).\n\n## Two `chat()` calls\n\nThe pause spans two runs. One user-visible turn. Two `chat()` calls.\n\n**Call 1 (pause).** `onInterruptBoundary` returns `{ interrupts }`. The run\nends with `RUN_FINISHED` and `outcome: interrupt`. The resolution hook does\nnot run.\n\n**Call 2 (resume).** The client starts a new request after\n`resolveInterrupt()` or `cancel()`. The body includes:\n\n- a new `runId`\n- `parentRunId` set to the paused run\n- `resume` with the answers. Each generic item also has `metadata` with the\n  original request (`tanstack:interruptContinuation`)\n\n`useChat` sends those fields for you. If you POST by hand, include all three.\nIf `resume` is present and `parentRunId` is missing, the server throws.\n\nA hand-built generic resume item looks like this:\n\n```ts\nimport { wrapGenericInterruptContinuation } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nconst resumeItem = {\n  interruptId: 'generic-1',\n  status: 'resolved' as const,\n  payload: { approved: true },\n  metadata: wrapGenericInterruptContinuation({\n    v: 1,\n    definitionId: 'review-plan',\n    key: 'turn-1',\n    batchIndex: 0,\n    reason: 'review',\n    message: 'Review the plan',\n  }),\n}\n```\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant Client\n    participant Server\n\n    Client->>Server: first chat() request\n    Server-->>Client: RUN_FINISHED outcome interrupt\n    Client->>User: interrupts array\n    User->>Client: resolveInterrupt or cancel\n    Client->>Server: second chat() with parentRunId and resume\n    Note over Server: onInterruptResolution runs here\n    Server-->>Client: continue, cancel tools, or stop\n```\n\n## Exact place in the second call\n\n```\nsetup\nonConfig                 (phase is init)\nonInterruptResolution    (phase is still init)\nonStart\nthen stop, or continue the agent loop\n```\n\nThe hook runs **once**, at the start of the continuation. It does not run at\n`beforeModel`, `afterModel`, `beforeTools`, or `afterTools`.\n\n`ctx.phase` is `'init'`. `ctx.iteration` is `0`. No model call has started.\n\nThe hook runs once per batch. Two cards in one pause still produce one hook\ncall with both answers.\n\nThe hook does not run on the first user message. It does not run for a\ntool-approval or client-tool batch that has no generic interrupt.\n\nIf that continuation pauses again, that is a third `chat()` call. The hook\nruns again at the start of that third call.\n\n## Read the typed answers\n\n```ts\nimport type { ChatMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { reviewPlan } from './interrupts'\n\nexport const applyReview: ChatMiddleware<unknown, typeof reviewPlan> = {\n  name: 'apply-review',\n  onInterruptResolution(_ctx, resumedInterrupts) {\n    for (const result of resumedInterrupts.for(reviewPlan)) {\n      if (result.status === 'resolved' && !result.response.approved) {\n        return { toolResume: 'stop' }\n      }\n    }\n  },\n}\n```\n\n- `resumedInterrupts.for(reviewPlan)` keeps the response type for that\n  definition\n- `resumedInterrupts.all()` returns every registered answer\n- `resumedInterrupts.all(reviewPlan, otherDefinition)` narrows to those\n  definitions\n\nEach item is `resolved` (with `response`) or `cancelled`.\n\n## What the hook can return\n\nReturn `toolResume` to decide what happens to **pending tools** from the\npaused turn:\n\n| Value | Effect |\n| --- | --- |\n| `continue` | Run the pending tools |\n| `cancel` | Mark the pending tools as cancelled. Do not run them |\n| `stop` | End the run after `onStart`. No tools. No model call |\n\nWhen more than one middleware returns a value, the engine keeps the stricter\none. `stop` wins over `cancel`. `cancel` wins over `continue`.\n\nIf a generic interrupt shares a batch with client tools, the client does not\nrun those client tools until `toolResume` is `continue`. `cancel` and `stop`\nskip them. After `continue`, the engine emits the client-tool wait again.\n\nAfter a `continue`, the engine picks up from the phase that paused:\n\n| First run paused at | Next step |\n| --- | --- |\n| `beforeModel` | The model call |\n| `afterModel` | Tools, if the model asked for them |\n| `beforeTools` | Tool execution |\n| `afterTools` | The next model turn (the tools already ran) |\n\n## What the hook cannot change\n\n`onInterruptResolution` cannot change config. It cannot change the model or\nthe adapter.\n\nThese fields change only from `onConfig` (or `onStructuredOutputConfig`):\n\n- `messages`\n- `systemPrompts`\n- `tools`\n- `modelOptions`\n- `metadata`\n\nThe user answer is **not** added to `messages` by itself. If the model must\nsee the note, you add it.\n\n## Apply the answer in `onConfig`\n\nOrder on the continuation:\n\n1. `onConfig` with `phase: 'init'`. The answers are not applied yet.\n2. `onInterruptResolution`. Read the answers and store them on the run.\n3. `onConfig` with `phase: 'beforeModel'`. Return the new prompts, tools, or\n   messages.\n\nStore the answer in a [middleware capability](../advanced/middleware#capabilities).\nThe value lives on `ctx` for this `chat()` call. Another middleware can\ndeclare `requires` and read the same note. Two overlapping `chat()` calls do\nnot share the value.\n\nIf you list the capability in `provides`, you must provide it in `setup`.\nYou do not have the user answer yet. Provide an empty box first. Write the\nanswer in `onInterruptResolution`.\n\n```ts\nimport { createCapability, type ChatMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { reviewPlan } from './interrupts'\n\nexport const reviewNote = createCapability<{ note?: string }>()('review-note')\nexport const [getReviewNote, provideReviewNote] = reviewNote\n\nexport const reviewMiddleware: ChatMiddleware<unknown, typeof reviewPlan> = {\n  name: 'review-plan',\n  provides: [reviewNote],\n  setup(ctx) {\n    provideReviewNote(ctx, {})\n  },\n  onInterruptBoundary(ctx) {\n    if (ctx.phase !== 'beforeModel') return\n    if (ctx.parentRunId) return\n    return {\n      interrupts: [\n        reviewPlan.interrupt({\n          key: 'initial-plan',\n          reason: 'review-required',\n          message: 'Review the proposed plan.',\n          payload: {\n            title: 'Release plan',\n            changes: ['Add search'],\n          },\n        }),\n      ],\n    }\n  },\n  onInterruptResolution(ctx, resumed) {\n    const [result] = resumed.for(reviewPlan)\n    if (result?.status !== 'resolved') return\n    provideReviewNote(ctx, { note: result.response.note })\n    if (!result.response.approved) {\n      return { toolResume: 'stop' }\n    }\n  },\n  onConfig(ctx, config) {\n    if (ctx.phase !== 'beforeModel') return\n    const note = getReviewNote(ctx).note\n    if (!note) return\n    return {\n      systemPrompts: [\n        ...config.systemPrompts,\n        `User review note: ${note}`,\n      ],\n    }\n  },\n}\n```\n\nRegister the object on `chat({ middleware: [reviewMiddleware] })`.\n\nA later middleware can read the same note:\n\n```ts\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { getReviewNote, reviewNote } from './review-plan'\n\nexport const applyVoice: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: 'apply-voice',\n  requires: [reviewNote],\n  onConfig(ctx, config) {\n    const note = getReviewNote(ctx).note\n    if (!note) return\n    return {\n      systemPrompts: [...config.systemPrompts, `Voice note: ${note}`],\n    }\n  },\n}\n```\n\nOther hooks that can change behavior, but not this resume payload:\n\n- `onBeforeToolCall` can rewrite args, skip a tool, or abort\n- `onChunk` can rewrite or drop stream events\n- `onShouldContinue` can return `false` to stop the loop with a normal finish\n\nSee [Middleware](../advanced/middleware) for those hooks.\n\n## Persistence\n\nWith [chat persistence](../persistence/chat-persistence), the hook still runs\nat the same moment: after init `onConfig`, before `onStart`.\n\nPersistence rebuilds the pending requests from the store and clears\n`config.resume` so the engine does not rebuild them from client history. You\nstill read answers from `resumedInterrupts.for(definition)`.\n\n## Register both sides\n\nThe continuation needs the same definitions and the same middleware as the\npaused run. Forward `parentRunId` and `resume` from the request.\n\n```ts\n// app/api/chat/route.ts\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { reviewMiddleware } from '../../chat-middleware'\nimport { reviewPlan } from '../../interrupts'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request)\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    threadId: params.threadId,\n    runId: params.runId,\n    ...(params.parentRunId ? { parentRunId: params.parentRunId } : {}),\n    ...(params.resume ? { resume: params.resume } : {}),\n    interrupts: [reviewPlan],\n    middleware: [reviewMiddleware],\n  })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Apply Answers\nid: interrupts-apply-answers\norder: 6\ndescription: \"Read a generic interrupt answer on the continuation run and apply it to the next model turn.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - onInterruptResolution\n  - toolResume\n  - generic interrupt\n  - parentRunId\n  - createCapability\n---\n\nThe user approved a plan or typed a note. You need that value on the server\nbefore the next model call. `onInterruptResolution` is where you read it. It\ndoes not change config. `onConfig` is where you apply it.\n\nBy the end of this page you know when the resolution hook runs, what it can\nreturn, and how to turn the answer into a prompt, a tool list, or a stop.\n\nDefine and emit the interrupt first. See [Generic Interrupts](./generic).\n\n## Two `chat()` calls\n\nThe pause spans two runs. One user-visible turn. Two `chat()` calls.\n\n**Call 1 (pause).** `onInterruptBoundary` returns `{ interrupts }`. The run\nends with `RUN_FINISHED` and `outcome: interrupt`. The resolution hook does\nnot run.\n\n**Call 2 (resume).** The client starts a new request after\n`resolveInterrupt()` or `cancel()`. The body includes:\n\n- a new `runId`\n- `parentRunId` set to the paused run\n- `resume` with the answers. Each generic item also has `metadata` with the\n  original request (`tanstack:interruptContinuation`)\n\n`useChat` sends those fields for you. If you POST by hand, include all three.\nIf `resume` is present and `parentRunId` is missing, the server throws.\n\nA hand-built generic resume item looks like this:\n\n```ts\nimport { wrapGenericInterruptContinuation } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nconst resumeItem = {\n  interruptId: 'generic-1',\n  status: 'resolved' as const,\n  payload: { approved: true },\n  metadata: wrapGenericInterruptContinuation({\n    v: 1,\n    definitionId: 'review-plan',\n    key: 'turn-1',\n    batchIndex: 0,\n    reason: 'review',\n    message: 'Review the plan',\n  }),\n}\n```\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant Client\n    participant Server\n\n    Client->>Server: first chat() request\n    Server-->>Client: RUN_FINISHED outcome interrupt\n    Client->>User: interrupts array\n    User->>Client: resolveInterrupt or cancel\n    Client->>Server: second chat() with parentRunId and resume\n    Note over Server: onInterruptResolution runs here\n    Server-->>Client: continue, cancel tools, or stop\n```\n\n## Exact place in the second call\n\n```\nsetup\nonConfig                 (phase is init)\nonInterruptResolution    (phase is still init)\nonStart\nthen stop, or continue the agent loop\n```\n\nThe hook runs **once**, at the start of the continuation. It does not run at\n`beforeModel`, `afterModel`, `beforeTools`, or `afterTools`.\n\n`ctx.phase` is `'init'`. `ctx.iteration` is `0`. No model call has started.\n\nThe hook runs once per batch. Two cards in one pause still produce one hook\ncall with both answers.\n\nThe hook does not run on the first user message. It does not run for a\ntool-approval or client-tool batch that has no generic interrupt.\n\nIf that continuation pauses again, that is a third `chat()` call. The hook\nruns again at the start of that third call.\n\n## Read the typed answers\n\n```ts\nimport type { ChatMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { reviewPlan } from './interrupts'\n\nexport const applyReview: ChatMiddleware<unknown, typeof reviewPlan> = {\n  name: 'apply-review',\n  onInterruptResolution(_ctx, resumedInterrupts) {\n    for (const result of resumedInterrupts.for(reviewPlan)) {\n      if (result.status === 'resolved' && !result.response.approved) {\n        return { toolResume: 'stop' }\n      }\n    }\n  },\n}\n```\n\n- `resumedInterrupts.for(reviewPlan)` keeps the response type for that\n  definition\n- `resumedInterrupts.all()` returns every registered answer\n- `resumedInterrupts.all(reviewPlan, otherDefinition)` narrows to those\n  definitions\n\nEach item is `resolved` (with `response`) or `cancelled`.\n\n## What the hook can return\n\nReturn `toolResume` to decide what happens to **pending tools** from the\npaused turn:\n\n| Value | Effect |\n| --- | --- |\n| `continue` | Run the pending tools |\n| `cancel` | Mark the pending tools as cancelled. Do not run them |\n| `stop` | End the run after `onStart`. No tools. No model call |\n\nWhen more than one middleware returns a value, the engine keeps the stricter\none. `stop` wins over `cancel`. `cancel` wins over `continue`.\n\nIf a generic interrupt shares a batch with client tools, the client does not\nrun those client tools until `toolResume` is `continue`. `cancel` and `stop`\nskip them. After `continue`, the engine emits the client-tool wait again.\n\nAfter a `continue`, the engine picks up from the phase that paused:\n\n| First run paused at | Next step |\n| --- | --- |\n| `beforeModel` | The model call |\n| `afterModel` | Tools, if the model asked for them |\n| `beforeTools` | Tool execution |\n| `afterTools` | The next model turn (the tools already ran) |\n\n## What the hook cannot change\n\n`onInterruptResolution` cannot change config. It cannot change the model or\nthe adapter.\n\nThese fields change only from `onConfig` (or `onStructuredOutputConfig`):\n\n- `messages`\n- `systemPrompts`\n- `tools`\n- `modelOptions`\n- `metadata`\n\nThe user answer is **not** added to `messages` by itself. If the model must\nsee the note, you add it.\n\n## Apply the answer in `onConfig`\n\nOrder on the continuation:\n\n1. `onConfig` with `phase: 'init'`. The answers are not applied yet.\n2. `onInterruptResolution`. Read the answers and store them on the run.\n3. `onConfig` with `phase: 'beforeModel'`. Return the new prompts, tools, or\n   messages.\n\nStore the answer in a [middleware capability](../advanced/middleware#capabilities).\nThe value lives on `ctx` for this `chat()` call. Another middleware can\ndeclare `requires` and read the same note. Two overlapping `chat()` calls do\nnot share the value.\n\nIf you list the capability in `provides`, you must provide it in `setup`.\nYou do not have the user answer yet. Provide an empty box first. Write the\nanswer in `onInterruptResolution`.\n\n```ts\nimport { createCapability, type ChatMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { reviewPlan } from './interrupts'\n\nexport const reviewNote = createCapability<{ note?: string }>()('review-note')\nexport const [getReviewNote, provideReviewNote] = reviewNote\n\nexport const reviewMiddleware: ChatMiddleware<unknown, typeof reviewPlan> = {\n  name: 'review-plan',\n  provides: [reviewNote],\n  setup(ctx) {\n    provideReviewNote(ctx, {})\n  },\n  onInterruptBoundary(ctx) {\n    if (ctx.phase !== 'beforeModel') return\n    if (ctx.parentRunId) return\n    return {\n      interrupts: [\n        reviewPlan.interrupt({\n          key: 'initial-plan',\n          reason: 'review-required',\n          message: 'Review the proposed plan.',\n          payload: {\n            title: 'Release plan',\n            changes: ['Add search'],\n          },\n        }),\n      ],\n    }\n  },\n  onInterruptResolution(ctx, resumed) {\n    const [result] = resumed.for(reviewPlan)\n    if (result?.status !== 'resolved') return\n    provideReviewNote(ctx, { note: result.response.note })\n    if (!result.response.approved) {\n      return { toolResume: 'stop' }\n    }\n  },\n  onConfig(ctx, config) {\n    if (ctx.phase !== 'beforeModel') return\n    const note = getReviewNote(ctx).note\n    if (!note) return\n    return {\n      systemPrompts: [\n        ...config.systemPrompts,\n        `User review note: ${note}`,\n      ],\n    }\n  },\n}\n```\n\nRegister the object on `chat({ middleware: [reviewMiddleware] })`.\n\nA later middleware can read the same note:\n\n```ts\nimport { type ChatMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { getReviewNote, reviewNote } from './review-plan'\n\nexport const applyVoice: ChatMiddleware = {\n  name: 'apply-voice',\n  requires: [reviewNote],\n  onConfig(ctx, config) {\n    const note = getReviewNote(ctx).note\n    if (!note) return\n    return {\n      systemPrompts: [...config.systemPrompts, `Voice note: ${note}`],\n    }\n  },\n}\n```\n\nOther hooks that can change behavior, but not this resume payload:\n\n- `onBeforeToolCall` can rewrite args, skip a tool, or abort\n- `onChunk` can rewrite or drop stream events\n- `onShouldContinue` can return `false` to stop the loop with a normal finish\n\nSee [Middleware](../advanced/middleware) for those hooks.\n\n## Persistence\n\nWith [chat persistence](../persistence/chat-persistence), the hook still runs\nat the same moment: after init `onConfig`, before `onStart`.\n\nPersistence rebuilds the pending requests from the store and clears\n`config.resume` so the engine does not rebuild them from client history. You\nstill read answers from `resumedInterrupts.for(definition)`.\n\n## Register both sides\n\nThe continuation needs the same definitions and the same middleware as the\npaused run. Forward `parentRunId` and `resume` from the request.\n\n```ts\n// app/api/chat/route.ts\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { reviewMiddleware } from '../../chat-middleware'\nimport { reviewPlan } from '../../interrupts'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request)\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    threadId: params.threadId,\n    runId: params.runId,\n    ...(params.parentRunId ? { parentRunId: params.parentRunId } : {}),\n    ...(params.resume ? { resume: params.resume } : {}),\n    interrupts: [reviewPlan],\n    middleware: [reviewMiddleware],\n  })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n"}
